# tests/qemu/block.ndb: the block class (docs/proto/block.md) and
# drv-virtio-blk (M5 step 1). The scenario gives QEMU a second disk of 64 MiB,
# made fresh for each run (disk=): devmgr matches both disks against
# boot/drv/virtio-blk.ndb and starts a driver for each, on /srv/disk0 (the boot
# disk) and /srv/disk1. blktest runs the protocol's conformance checks
# against disk1, and against the two partitions on it, which partd serves as
# windows (tests/user/blkparts.ndb); then it kills the drivers, and reads back
# through a new session what it wrote before. partd and blktest start
# together, so only partd's line is waited for before blktest's ok. netd and
# the shell are skipped: nothing here needs them.

scenario=block timeout=40 cmdline=vx.skip=rc,netd with=blktest,blkparts disk=64
expect="drv-virtio-blk: 64 MiB, 512-byte sectors"
expect="partd: /srv/disk1: 2 partitions"
expect="blktest: ok"
expect="blktest: stopped the drivers; the session ended"
expect="devmgr: started drv-virtio-blk"
expect=" checks, 0 failed"
fail="vx: panic"
fail="FAILED"
fail=") killed: "
